2025-05-05 00:25:59 - Thread-156 (execute) - INFO - [Corrected SQL]
Thinking process:  
We need to count (a) the total number of patents granted between 2010-01-01 and 2018-12-31 and (b) how many of those patents contain at least one backward citation whose JSON field "category" includes the string ‘SEA’.  
Snowflake cannot use an OUTER (LEFT) join with a table function, so instead we place LATERAL FLATTEN directly in the FROM clause with the option OUTER => TRUE. This keeps rows that have an empty or NULL citation array (f.value is NULL) while still expanding existing arrays. We then use COUNT(DISTINCT …) for the totals, and a CASE expression inside another COUNT(DISTINCT …) to isolate the SEA-cited patents.

```sql
--Description: Count granted patents (2010-2018) and how many have at least one 'SEA' backward citation
SELECT
    COUNT(DISTINCT p."publication_number")                                                             AS "total_grants_2010_2018",
    COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN f.value:"category"::STRING ILIKE '%SEA%' THEN p."publication_number" END) AS "with_sea_citations"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation", OUTER => TRUE) f
WHERE p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20100101 AND 20181231;
```
